160
00:09:12,390 --> 00:09:15,730
So let's talk a little
bit about the pathogenesis

161
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:18,990
of primary hypertension.
So largely it's

162
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:23,450
related to either an
increased cardiac output

163
00:09:23,450 --> 00:09:26,110
or increased total
peripheral resistance. So

164
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:28,390
if you guys remember
your physiology formulas,

165
00:09:28,590 --> 00:09:31,250
mean arterial pressure
equals cardiac output

166
00:09:31,250 --> 00:09:33,670
times total peripheral
resistance. So

167
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:36,090
increasing that cardiac
output or increasing that

168
00:09:36,090 --> 00:09:38,210
total peripheral
resistance is going to

169
00:09:38,210 --> 00:09:40,210
lead to an increased
mean arterial pressure.

170
00:09:40,790 --> 00:09:43,150
Then we have cardiac
output equals heart rate

171
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:46,030
times stroke volume. So
again, if you increase

172
00:09:46,030 --> 00:09:48,090
the heart rate or if
you increase the stroke

173
00:09:48,090 --> 00:09:50,870
value, you increase
the cardiac output and

174
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:52,910
in turn increase the
mean arterial pressure.

175
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:55,940
So a lot of this stems
from the renin angiotensin

176
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:58,690
aldosterone system. So
we'll quickly review

177
00:09:58,690 --> 00:10:01,410
that and how that happens
and leads to increased

178
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:04,330
blood pressure. So you
have angiotensinogen that's

179
00:10:04,330 --> 00:10:08,750
converted into angiotensin
1 from renin. And

180
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:10,450
things that are going to
stimulate renin are going

181
00:10:10,450 --> 00:10:12,530
to be detection of
decreased blood pressure,

182
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:15,010
decreased sodium delivery
to the macula dents of

183
00:10:15,010 --> 00:10:18,760
the kidney, and increased
sympathetics. So then

184
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:23,770
angiotensin 1 gets converted
to angiotensin 2 from

185
00:10:23,770 --> 00:10:27,050
angiotensin converting
enzyme. And then And

186
00:10:27,050 --> 00:10:30,790
angiotensin 2 has a couple
of different effects on

187
00:10:30,790 --> 00:10:33,930
the body. So the first is
increasing sympathetics.

188
00:10:33,970 --> 00:10:37,650
So increased sympathetics
is going to lead to

189
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:40,720
increased heart rate.
It leads to increased

190
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:43,050
contractility, which will
increase the stroke volume.

191
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:45,090
And so increased heart
rate and increased stroke

192
00:10:45,090 --> 00:10:47,410
volume are going to
increase the cardiac output.

193
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:51,150
Then angiotensin 2 could
also increase aldosterone

194
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:54,350
secretion from the adrenal
glands and increased

195
00:10:54,350 --> 00:10:56,510
anti-diuretic hormone
release from the posterior

196
00:10:56,510 --> 00:11:00,410
pituitary of the hypothalamus.
So both of these things

197
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:03,730
are going to increase
sodium and water retention

198
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:07,710
in the vasculature system,
and that's going to

199
00:11:07,710 --> 00:11:10,990
increase blood volume, and
that's going to increase

200
00:11:10,990 --> 00:11:15,270
preload, which increases
stroke volume and leads to

201
00:11:15,270 --> 00:11:18,050
increased cardiac output.
So all of these things

202
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:20,310
are going to lead to an
increased blood pressure.

203
00:11:22,930 --> 00:11:23,790
Additionally,

204
00:11:23,910 --> 00:11:26,690
all of these things, so
the increased angiotensin

205
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:29,830
2, increased sympathetics,
increased antidiuretic

206
00:11:29,830 --> 00:11:32,630
hormone, increased
aldosterone, they lead

207
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:35,290
to more vasoconstriction,
and that's going to

208
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:37,370
lead to increased total
peripheral resistance.

209
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,850
And like we mentioned
before, that directly

210
00:11:39,850 --> 00:11:41,650
leads to an increased
blood pressure.

211
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,910
Now, increased blood
pressure in and of

212
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:46,710
itself causes some
vascular remodeling,

213
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:50,090
increased endothelin,
decreased vasodilators.

214
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:53,880
So that's going to lead to
further vasoconstriction,

215
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:57,630
which further increases that
total peripheral resistance,

216
00:11:57,630 --> 00:12:00,030
leading to even more
increased blood pressure.

217
00:12:01,990 --> 00:12:04,930
So next we'll talk about
secondary hypertension.

218
00:12:04,930 --> 00:12:07,850
This is going to account
for the remaining 10

219
00:12:07,850 --> 00:12:10,170
% of hypertension, and
it's considered to be

220
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:12,950
